    "evidence_text": "Annotated phenotypes include treatment non-adherence, chronic pain, advanced/metastatic\n\ncancer, as well as 10 other phenotypes.\n\nAs EHRs act to streamline the\n\npublicly available MIMIC database .\n\nThese variables are sufficient to use the data set\n\nTable defines each of the considered clinical patient phenotypes.\n\nTable counts the occurrences of these phenotypes across patient notes and Figure contains the corresponding correlation matrix.\n\nThe operators within each team were instructed to\n\nwork independently on note annotation.\n\nLimitations\tThere exist a few limitations to this database.\n\nand models resulting from these data may not generalize to notes generated at other hospitals.\n\nTable summarizes the calculated Cohen's Kappa coefficients.\n\nThis corpus can also be accessed on GitHub after completing all of the above requirements.\n\nEach of the baseline model is a binary classifier indicating whether a given phenotype is present in the input patient note.\n\nAs a result, we train a separate model for each phenotype.\n\noverfitting .\n\nThe model was optimized with adadelta .\n\nEach patient note was annotated by at least one clinical researcher and one resident physician for 13 high-context patient phenotypes.",
